.env
__pycache__/
*.pyc
data/screener_cache.db
.streamlit/secrets.toml
.venv/
.venv-secfsdstools/
# Rollback copy of the pre-2026-08-10 environment (149 packages). Ignored for the
# same reason as .venv/ - it is a virtualenv, not source. Without this rule a
# `git add -A` stages ~15,000 site-packages files.
.venv-OLD/

# Wealthsimple export — live OAuth session + real trade history, never commit
tools/session.json
tools/ws_import_*.json
tools/needs_review.json
tools/account_balances.json
tools/open_positions.json
tools/*.tmp

# data/ and scripts/ — REAL BROKERAGE DATA, never commit.
#
# These were protected only by remembering to `git add` explicit paths, which is
# not protection. data/ holds a 208-row options trade ledger with per-trade P&L
# and a ws_fills_json column, 208 Wealthsimple order JSONs under
# options_price_paths/, a contract-spec map, and cached underlying bars; scripts/
# holds the analysis code that produced them. Same category as the tools/ rules
# above, which already block the Wealthsimple exports by name.
#
# Deliberately whole-directory rather than file-by-file: the exposure is not a
# fixed list of filenames, it is "whatever those scripts write next", and a
# per-file rule protects only the files that happened to exist when it was
# written. Nothing under either path is tracked (verified: `git ls-files data/
# scripts/` returns 0), so this hides nothing that git was showing as trackable.
#
# Note data/scan_jobs/ was already ignored above, so scan checkpoints and the
# ARCHIVED_*.csv.bak evidence files were never visible in `git status` anyway —
# this rule does not change their status. To track something under these paths
# in future, `git add -f <path>` still works.
#
# LEADING SLASH IS LOAD-BEARING. A bare `data/` matches a directory of that name
# at ANY depth, which silently shadowed two tracked files under
# .claude/agents/data/. Anchored to the repo root, it matches only the two
# directories intended.
/data/
/scripts/

# secfsdstools config — contains contact email; copy from .secfsdstools.cfg.example
.secfsdstools.cfg

# background scan job checkpoints (runtime artifacts)
data/scan_jobs/

# SEC ticker->CIK map cached by code33/ticker_lookup.py (~1MB, regenerable,
# refreshes itself weekly)
data/company_tickers.json

# News Scanner session history — today's headlines only, cleared on the first
# request of a new calendar day. Pure runtime state, plus the user's watchlist.
data/news_session.db
data/news_session.db-wal
data/news_session.db-shm
